! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.5, "CONTINUED FRACTION EVALUATION", printed pp.29-30
! (PDF 30-31), read in the ink.
!
!   "Evaluate the continued fraction
!        F = x / (1 - x**2 / (3 - x**2 / (5 - x**2 / (7 - ...
!                                              - x**2 / 39))))
!   with x = pi/4."
!
!   Method 1.
!       CONF    L(U), X
!               *, X
!               ST(U), TEMP             'x**2
!               LX, $2, XW2
!               L(U), NUM               '39
!       LOOP    R/N, TEMP               'X*X/39
!               ST, TEMP1
!               L(U), NUM
!               -, TWO
!               ST(U), NUM
!               +, TEMP1                '37-X*X/39     [p.30 from the CB]
!               CB, $2, LOOP
!               R/, X
!               ST(U), TEMP2
!               BEW, $
!       X       DD(N), $PI/4
!       NUM     DD(N), 39.0
!       TWO     DD(N), 2.0
!       XW2     XW, 0.0, 19, XW2
!       TEMP    DR(N), (3)
!       TEMP1   SYN(N), TEMP+1.0
!       TEMP2   SYN(N), TEMP+2.0
!
! The twenty-two printed statements are the deck's last twenty-two, as
! printed, data and all.  BLOCK A before them is the deck's copy of the
! fifteen instructions with NUM, TWO, XW2, TEMP, TEMP1, TEMP2 and LOOP
! renamed (an A appended), the BEW left off, and its own constants
! written "39" and "2", which the assembler makes exact; see below.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2.  strap_asm.py refuses "*, X" and the six
! others like it; decks/problem_3_bare_op_symbol_dds.strap.  The page's
! own comment (c) is the rule the host STRAP II follows: no dds written,
! so "the dds of the rightmost symbolic address" -- every one here is
! (N) -- and the operations are normalized floating point.  "R/N" is
! RECIPROCAL DIVIDE with the negative sign modifier, which comment (b)
! says "should not be confused with R/(N)".
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES.  TEMP = x**2.  With the accumulator holding the
! running denominator d (39 to begin), R/N, TEMP makes -x**2/d
! (Reference Manual printed p.94: "The operand specified by the
! effective address, the dividend, is divided by the operand in the
! left half of the accumulator ... The sign of the dividend is modified
! by the sign modifiers"), NUM steps down by two, and the sum is the
! next denominator.  Nineteen times: 37, 35, ... 1.  Then R/, X is x/d.
! The fraction is tan x, so F = tan(pi/4) = 1 and the last TEMP1 is
! -(1 - pi/4) = -0.2146018366025517.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE DERIVED FROM THE MANUAL'S RULES, NOT FROM THE
! MODEL, by tests/problem_3_expected.py (p35); the rules and pages are
! in its header.  About sixty truncating steps.
!
!   BLOCK A, exact 39 and 2:
!     TEMP2A   000FFFFFFFFFFFE0   0.9999999999999929   F: 1, two units
!                                 of the 48th place short, the way
!                                 truncation errs
!     NUMA     0028000000000000   exactly 1 = 39 - 19 x 2, by hand:
!                                 integers, every subtraction exact
!     TEMPA    0009DE9E64DF22D0   0.6168502750680780   x**2
!                                 ((pi/4)**2 = 0.6168502750680849)
!     TEMP1A   005DBC095777A5B8   -0.2146018366025499  -(1 - pi/4),
!                                 sign bit on
!
!   THE PAGE, with 39.0 and 2.0 as the host STRAP II makes them, each
!   one unit of its 48th place short (39 - 2**-42, 2 - 2**-47; see
!   problem_3_4_method1.strap):
!     TEMP2    00280000000002A0   1.0000000000002984
!     NUM      000FFFFFFFFFFC20   0.9999999999997797
!     TEMP     0009DE9E64DF22D0
!     TEMP1    005DBC095777A6E8   -0.2146018366025668
!     X_as_assembled 000C90FDAA221680, TWO_as_assembled 002FFFFFFFFFFFF0
!   NUM by hand.  39 - 2**-42 less 2 - 2**-47 is 37 - 2**-42 + 2**-47,
!   and the result is truncated to 48 bits.  While the result is 2 or
!   more its 48th place is 2**-46 or coarser, so the 2**-47 is dropped
!   every time and the 2**-42 is kept: 37 - 2**-42, 35 - 2**-42, ...
!   3 - 2**-42 after eighteen steps.  The nineteenth result is below 1,
!   its 48th place is 2**-48, and the 2**-47 survives once:
!   NUM = 1 - 2**-42 + 2**-47 = 1 - 62 x 2**-48, fraction FFFFFFFFFFC2,
!   exponent 0: 000FFFFFFFFFFC20.  The calculator agrees.
!   So the page's F is 3 x 10**-13 above 1 where block A's is 7 x
!   10**-15 below: what the one-unit-short constants cost.  WHICH THE
!   7030's STRAP DID IS NOT DECIDED BY ANY PRINTED WORD
!   (tests/check_strap2_dd.py); the model is checked against both.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): "TWOA DD(N), 2" changed to "TWOA DD(N), 3".
! FAIL A_F, A_NUM and A_TEMP1; A_TEMP, the six checks of the page's own
! block and the PC passed.

! --- block A: the deck's copy, exact constants ------------------------
CONFA   L(U), X
        *, X
        ST(U), TEMPA
        LX, $2, XW2A
        L(U), NUMA
LOOPA   R/N, TEMPA
        ST, TEMP1A
        L(U), NUMA
        -, TWOA
        ST(U), NUMA
        +, TEMP1A
        CB, $2, LOOPA
        R/, X
        ST(U), TEMP2A
! --- the page, as printed -------------------------------------------
CONF    L(U), X
        *, X
        ST(U), TEMP
        LX, $2, XW2
        L(U), NUM
LOOP    R/N, TEMP
        ST, TEMP1
        L(U), NUM
        -, TWO
        ST(U), NUM
        +, TEMP1
        CB, $2, LOOP
        R/, X
        ST(U), TEMP2
        BEW, $
X       DD(N), $PI/4
NUM     DD(N), 39.0
TWO     DD(N), 2.0
XW2     XW, 0.0, 19, XW2
TEMP    DR(N), (3)
TEMP1   SYN(N), TEMP+1.0
TEMP2   SYN(N), TEMP+2.0
! --- block A's data -------------------------------------------------
NUMA    DD(N), 39
TWOA    DD(N), 2
XW2A    XW, 0.0, 19, XW2A
TEMPA   DR(N), (3)
TEMP1A  SYN(N), TEMPA+1.0
TEMP2A  SYN(N), TEMPA+2.0
        END, CONFA
